// Víbora Padel service worker: makes the installed app (and the site) work offline.
//
// - Install: precaches the app shell, every module, the MediaPipe runtime and the default
//   'full' pose model, hands, fonts and icons (PRECACHE, generated by tools/precache.mjs with a
//   content hash per file). Files whose hash did not change are copied from the previous
//   version's cache instead of downloaded again, so an update only fetches what changed.
// - Fetch, same-origin requests inside the scope only (everything else, e.g. the googleapis
//   telemetry that src/app/privacy.js blocks, is never touched or cached):
//     * pages, src/, styles/, the manifest: network first (revalidated, 4 s timeout), cache
//       fallback, so updates arrive as soon as they are deployed and the app still opens offline;
//     * vendor/, models/, assets/, fonts/, icons/: cache first (immutable), filled at runtime for
//       files outside the precache (the lite / heavy models, the non-SIMD wasm build).
// - Activate: deletes caches of older versions and claims open pages.
// - Messages: 'SKIP_WAITING' (the page's "Update ready — restart"), 'CACHE_URLS' (the page lists
//   what it loaded on the first visit, before this worker controlled it), 'STATUS'.
// All paths are relative to this file, so it works from a GitHub Pages sub-path.

